  "limitations": [
    "COCO val2017 consists of Flickr photographs, not dash-cam video: viewpoint, object scale, motion blur and compression differ from DreamDrive's uploaded videos, so these numbers do not transfer to road footage.",
    "RF-DETR-N was trained on COCO train2017; val2017 is its standard held-out split (no overlap with training images), but the label taxonomy and photographic style are in-domain for it and favour it.",
    "YOLOPv2 'vehicle' (BDD100K-trained, single class) is scored against merged COCO car+bus+truck as a cross-dataset check; the datasets use different labelling conventions (e.g. what counts as a vehicle, occlusion and truncation rules), so its AP is indicative only.",
    "Scored at the production confidence threshold through the production /v1/infer path; detections below that threshold never reach the app, so AP is computed on a truncated precision-recall curve and is not comparable with leaderboard numbers that use a 0.001 threshold.",
    "Lane-line and drivable-area accuracy are not evaluated: no openly licensed labels are available here (BDD100K requires owner registration).",
    "Traffic-light colour (red/yellow/green) is an HSV heuristic and is not evaluated; general traffic signs other than stop signs are unsupported.",
    "Images are JPEG-decoded, then re-encoded at quality 95 before inference (same as the video pipeline), so each image is compressed twice."
  ],
